    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** providing the core offensive upside, despite facing the formidable Shane McClanahan. Even with the lefty-on-lefty dynamic, **Gunnar Henderson** (66.87) and **Coby Mayo** (62.51) maintain high efficiency ratings primarily due to favorable park factors and high-leverage order placement. While **Liam Hicks** (59.92) and **Jackson Merrill** (58.97) fall just short of the 60+ \"Strong\" threshold, both are high-floor plays bolstered by strong platoon advantages against Brandon Young and Dean Kremer, respectively. **Wade Meckler** remains a vital engine at the top of the order; his score (52.77) is insulated by an elite projected SP matchup against Cody Bradford, helping to mitigate the inherent risk of his L/L platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Nasim Nunez** on the bench despite his speed profile, which usually commands a premium in our pursuit of SB category dominance. Ultimately, **Nasim Nunez** (47.63) could not overcome the efficiency floor set by **Luis Lara** (49.10) and **Andy Pages** (53.68). **Miguel Vargas** also surfaced as a strong candidate, but the optimizer favored the positional flexibility provided by the starters. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Liam Hicks**, **Tommy White**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Coby Mayo**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Wade Meckler**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages**; any shuffle in the batting order, particularly for **Sam Antonacci** or **Wade Meckler**, could shift their efficiency scores significantly. Additionally, while **Drake Baldwin** faces an elite arm in Henderson with an xERA of 2.90, his lead-off spot remains crucial for our R and RBI production. As always, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to navigate the remainder of the week without his production.",
